 Gorr — The God Butcher-

Movie: Thor: Love and Thunder
Origin: Unknown alien civilization
Role: God killer
Power Level: ⭐⭐⭐⭐½ 8.5/10

Introduction
Gorr begins as a believer who loses everything. His daughter's death destroys his faith and turns him against the gods.

Main Motivation
Protect children from uncaring gods.
Destroy gods who abuse their power.
Revenge against the gods.
His motivation comes from grief rather than greed.
Powers
With the Necrosword:

Superhuman strength
Enhanced durability
Shadow manipulation
Shadow creatures
Teleportation
God-killing ability
Necrosword powers
Major Examples
Hunts gods across the universe.
Defeats powerful divine beings.
Fights Thor and other powerful heroes.
Comes close to achieving his goal of killing countless gods.
Sacrifice
His greatest sacrifice is his daughter. His entire campaign begins because of her death.

Ultimately, he also gives up his own life to bring her back.

Why He Is Wrong
His pain is real, and some of his criticism of gods is understandable, but he turns grief into mass violence and decides that every god deserves death.

